from e import *
E(6,'hamara-bharat-incredible-india','Hamara Bharat: Incredible India!',
 ('A video call across India','Imagine a big screen showing smiling children from different states, each proudly showing you a craft from their home. That is exactly what happens in this chapter. It opens with a short passage about India and then takes you into the Ek Bharat, Shreshtha Bharat programme.'),
 [('The opening passage',['Bharat has been known across the world as a land of wise and heroic people. Its rich and varied culture has attracted travellers since ancient times.','The people here live in unison, which means together in harmony. This shows unity in diversity to the world.','Bharat has rivers, lakes and high mountains, and green forests with many plants, insects, birds and animals. These keep the country prosperous and respected.','The advice to everyone is that, as inhabitants, we need to keep working hard so that Bharat continues to prosper.']),
  ('Ek Bharat, Shreshtha Bharat',['In the story, a teacher asks students in a big hall if they are ready to meet friends from all over the country. The programme is called Ek Bharat, Shreshtha Bharat.','Renu explains that it is to know that we all belong to one nation and share a bond, and that our unity in diversity makes us a wonderful country.','The programme aims to improve interaction and mutual understanding between people of different states and union territories by pairing them. It celebrates unity in diversity and strengthens emotional bonds.','It aims to give people a sense of common identity by sharing best practices and experiences, and to contribute to nation building by showing how connected our cultures are.']),
  ('Aipan from Uttarakhand',['Akanksha from Uttarakhand tells about Aipan, a folk art drawn on family functions and festivals.','It is done with white rice flour paste on brick-red walls coloured with geru, a red clay. It is made on floors and walls of puja rooms and outside the main door.','It is an art made by the women of the family. The designs are beautiful and mathematical and based on cultural traditions and observations of nature.']),
  ('Dhokra from Odisha',['Priyaranjan from Odisha belongs to a tribe that practises Dhokra, a four-thousand-year-old metal craft.','First a figure is made of clay and dried, then covered with a layer of wax and the fine details are carved on the wax.','The figure is covered with clay and put in the fire. The wax melts and flows out through small openings.','Then melted brass scrap is poured into the empty space and takes the shape of the wax. At last the outer clay is removed and the metal figure is finished.']),
  ('Coconut shell craft from Kerala',['Chitra from Kerala describes coconut shell craft. First a brown coconut shell is cleaned inside and out, then made smooth with sandpaper or a machine.','Next it is shaped as wished and a base is fixed so that it is stable. At last it is polished with wood polish to make it shine.','Bowls, household things and even jewellery are made. It is a biodegradable craft, which means it will not harm the environment.']),
  ('Kondapalli toys from Andhra Pradesh',['Balamurali from Kondapalli village tells about a four-hundred-year-old toy-making art.','Soft wood from nearby hills is used. Each part of the toy is carved separately and pieces are joined with makku, a paste of tamarind seed powder and sawdust.','Details are added and finally the toys are coloured with oil and watercolours or vegetable dyes and enamel paints.','The toys show folk stories, animals, birds, bullock carts and rural life. Kondapalli toys and coconut shell craft both use natural materials from nature.']),
  ('Sequence words and the present tense',['To give steps in order, use to begin, first, then, next, after that, finally and at last. Example: first I get up, then I wear my uniform, next I eat, after that I wear my shoes, and finally I pick up my bag.','The children speak in the simple present tense, which tells about regular actions. With he, she and it we add s or es to the verb.','Examples: I know how to dance, he speaks very loudly, she draws paintings, they practise spellings on Friday.']),
  ('Speaking, writing and exploring',['Speak about a local art form of your region such as painting, rangoli, metal craft, embroidery, music, dance or drama. Say its name, what is needed and how it is made, using first, after that, next, then and at last.','Write a paragraph of five sentences about the art form you liked best and give your reasons.','Madhubani painting is a traditional art form from Bihar. Natural colours can be made from haldi for yellow, leaves for green, flowers or geru for red, and indigo for blue.','In the listening passage, gakkad bharta is made by roasting dough balls and brinjal and tomatoes, then serving crumbled gakkad with bharta and ghee.'])],
 [('Put the steps of making a Dhokra figure in order.',[('Start with the clay figure and wax layer.','The first stage makes the model.'),('Carve details, cover with clay, fire it so wax melts, pour in melted brass, and finally remove the clay.','Pouring brass in the place of wax is the key step.')]),
  ('Write present tense sentences with he, she, it: she / draw / paintings.',[('With she we use the verb with s or es.','Third person singular needs an s.'),('She draws paintings in free periods.','Draws has the s.')])],
 ('Choose one craft from the chapter and explain how it is made, using sequence words.',['Name the craft and the state.','List the materials.','Describe the steps with first, next, then and finally.','Say what is made from it.'],['All the crafts are made by machines.','Aipan is made on paper with paint.']),
 ['Bharat is rich in culture, rivers, forests and people who live in unison.','Ek Bharat, Shreshtha Bharat celebrates unity in diversity through state pairing.','Aipan, Dhokra, coconut shell craft and Kondapalli toys are traditional crafts.','Sequence words show the order of steps.','The present tense tells about regular actions, and he, she, it take s or es.'],
 [('m','What is Aipan made with?','White rice flour paste',[('Metal','Metal is used in Dhokra.'),('Wood','Wood is used in Kondapalli toys.')],'Aipan is made with rice paste on geru-coloured walls.'),
  ('m','Which state is Dhokra from, in the chapter?','Odisha',[('Kerala','Kerala has the coconut shell craft.'),('Bihar','Bihar has Madhubani painting.')],'Priyaranjan from Odisha tells about it.'),
  ('m','What is used to melt out of the clay mould in Dhokra?','Wax',[('Brass','Brass is poured in after the wax melts out.'),('Water','Wax melts out.')],'The wax melts and flows out through small openings.'),
  ('m','Why is coconut shell craft called biodegradable?','It will not harm the environment',[('It is made of metal','Coconut shell is not metal.'),('It is very expensive','Cost is not mentioned.')],'It breaks down naturally.'),
  ('m','What is makku in Kondapalli toys?','A paste of tamarind seed powder and sawdust',[('A kind of wood','Makku is the paste that joins parts.'),('A paint','Makku is a glue-like paste.')],'It is used to join the pieces.'),
  ('m','What is the aim of Ek Bharat, Shreshtha Bharat?','To celebrate unity in diversity',[('To hold sports matches','It is about culture and understanding.'),('To close schools','This is not the aim.')],'It pairs states and union territories.'),
  ('m','Which sentence uses the present tense correctly?','She draws a picture every day.',[('She draw a picture every day.','With she the verb needs s.'),('She drawing a picture every day.','This is incomplete.')],'He, she and it take s or es.'),
  ('m','Which word shows order of steps?','finally',[('colour','Colour does not show order.'),('toys','Toys is a noun.')],'Finally is a sequence word.'),
  ('s','Name one state-wise craft from the chapter.',['aipan','dhokra','coconut shell','kondapalli','madhubani'],'The chapter describes Aipan, Dhokra, coconut shell craft and Kondapalli toys.'),
  ('t','Unity in diversity means everyone must be the same.',False,'It means different people live together in harmony.')],
 keep=['unity in diversity','folk art','biodegradable'])
